## ERPForAll addon development

Before writing or changing an ERPForAll addon, read the matching skill file (each starts with a
short procedure and ends with its sources). The skills live in `{{KIT}}/skills/`.

- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-addon-tests/SKILL.md`: Test an ERPForAll addon - static lint, install into a database, native Rust tests with erp_testkit::Harness and registry builds, manifest consistency tests, and Elang component tests for client code. Use when asked to verify an addon works, add tests, or debug a failing install.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-attachments/SKILL.md`: Attach files to records from a native ERPForAll addon with the base attachments API (erp_addon_base::attachments) - staged uploads, create and create_unique, composer files claimed with adopt, for_record and open, the /erp/content/<id> route, reattach, copy, unlink with the record, who may see a file, the attachment size setting and the errors you will meet. Use when an addon must store, list, serve or move files that belong to a record.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-chatter/SKILL.md`: Add the chatter (messages, followers, activities, record history) to a model and its form in an ERPForAll addon - depend on mail, inherit mail.thread, place <chatter/> in the form view, track field changes, post messages from code, or give another addon's model a chatter through a bridge addon. Use when a record needs a discussion thread, followers, notes or a change history.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-client-extensions/SKILL.md`: Add web client code to an ERPForAll addon - a custom field widget, a control-panel extension, templates and styles declared in static/client.json, registries and patches in the Elang client. Use when a view needs a widget or UI behaviour that the built-in widgets do not give.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-create-addon/SKILL.md`: Create a new ERPForAll addon from scratch - manifest.toml, directory layout, data-only versus native (Rust) addon, scaffolding, listing data files, installing it into a database. Use when the user asks to start, scaffold or register a new ERPForAll addon or module.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-data-files/SKILL.md`: Write ERPForAll data files - XML records, external ids, ref/eval/search values, noupdate, CSV files, default data every model must ship, and demo data. Use when adding seed or default records, demo records, or when a data file fails to load.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-dynamic-reports/SKILL.md`: Build an on-screen dynamic report in an ERPForAll addon with the report engine (addon reporting) - a report as data (reporting.report, line, column and expression records with aggregate, formula and native engines), a native ReportProvider in Rust (lines, expand with paging, drill, init_options), typed cells, caret items and drill actions, and the client action that opens it. Use when the user wants a ledger, balance, aging or analysis screen with dates, comparison, unfolding, totals and drill-down. Printed PDF documents are the erpforall-reports skill.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-extend-addon/SKILL.md`: Extend an existing ERPForAll addon from a new addon - add fields to someone else's model, add a column or field to their form, add access rows, without editing the original. Use for requests like "add a field to the contact form" or "customize the product addon".
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-for-odoo-developers/SKILL.md`: Map Odoo concepts to ERPForAll - manifest, models, inheritance, api decorators, access rows and rules, views, data files, server actions, RPC, tracking, properties, settings, sudo, reports - and the places where ERPForAll deliberately differs or fails loudly. Use when the user knows Odoo and asks how to do something the ERPForAll way.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-jobs/SKILL.md`: Declare and enqueue durable background jobs in an ERPForAll addon - JobKindDecl and register_job_kind!, chunked StepArgs / StepOutcome model methods, EnqueueRequest with deduplication and singleton keys, job_cancel_by_key, JobHandler chunk_items isolation, and extending another addon's job step. Use when work should run asynchronously in short transactions or on a schedule.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-knowledge-graph/SKILL.md`: Look up what your own ERPForAll addons define before you write against it - models, fields, RPC methods, views, menus, actions, access rows, inheritance and addon dependencies, each with a file and line - and what a change to a file can affect. Use before naming a model or field in a view, an access row or a client call, before extending another addon, and before finishing a change.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-menus-actions/SKILL.md`: Add menus and window actions to an ERPForAll addon - ir.actions.act_window records, view_mode, linking specific views, <menuitem> trees, groups, icons, root menus and settings entries. Use when the user wants an app menu, a menu entry, or an action that opens a model's list or form.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-migrations/SKILL.md`: Write ERPForAll schema and data migrations for an addon upgrade - pre, post and end stages, #[erp_sdk::migration] Rust functions, migrations/<version>/<stage>-*.sql scripts, 0.0.0 every-upgrade hooks, adopting company-dependent fields, and upgrade tests. Use when bumping an addon's manifest version or migrating existing tables and records.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-models-fields/SKILL.md`: Declare ERPForAll models and fields - TOML model files for data-only addons and the #[model] / #[field] / #[extend] macros for native Rust addons, field types and keys, relations, defaults, constraints and computed fields, binary and image fields, company-dependent fields. Use when adding or changing a model, a field or a relation in an addon.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-orm-scale/SKILL.md`: Use ERPForAll's scale and search primitives in a native addon - business keys (UNIQUE NULLS NOT DISTINCT), batch Upsert with update and accumulate/accumulate_floor, optimistic concurrency with row_version and expect_versions, and bounded #[search_method] domain providers for nonstored computed fields. Use when maintaining balances, counters, idempotent batch imports, conflict-checked edits, or searchable computed fields.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-reports/SKILL.md`: Add a printed report to an ERPForAll addon - QWeb report templates, the ir.actions.report record that puts it under the Print menu, the print profile (the closed set of tags, classes, styles and directives a report may use), images, and business documents (invoice, order, slip) built from the shared document parts of the web addon. Use when the user asks for a PDF, a printout, a Print menu entry or a printed document of a model.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-review/SKILL.md`: Review an ERPForAll addon before committing or opening a pull request - pre-review checklist for manifest and data files, fail-loudly error handling, access rows and company_access, migrations, views and client code, tests, and optional specialist review lenses (Rust, SQL, security, UI). Use when finishing an addon task or auditing an addon diff.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-security/SKILL.md`: Set access control for an ERPForAll addon - security/ir.access.csv rows (permissions and restrictions), res.groups records, field-level groups, record domains with user.id and company_ids, company_access declarations, scoped elevation instead of sudo, user-writable preferences. Use when a model needs access rights, per-user or per-company record rules, a custom group, or code that must read past the user's rights.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-settings/SKILL.md`: Make a value of an ERPForAll addon configurable instead of hardcoding it - declare a Settings page entry (SettingDecl, global or company scope) or a technical system parameter (ParameterDecl) with a default, a floor and a hard bound, give the addon its own settings page, contribute settings to another app, read the values from Rust code. Use when an addon needs a limit, interval, switch, default choice or credential that an administrator may change.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-views/SKILL.md`: Write ERPForAll views - list, form and search XML in ir.ui.view records under the <erp> root, header buttons, groups and notebooks, field widgets, one2many line views, list dashboards and column widths, kanban, pivot, graph and calendar views, dashboard cards, and extending another addon's view with xpath/position inheritance. Use when adding or changing a screen, a column, a filter, a form layout or a board.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-wasm-addons/SKILL.md`: Build a light ERPForAll addon as a WebAssembly package - the same Rust source as a native addon compiled to a sandboxed component, export_component!, model_ref! to extend a data-only addon's model, what a component body may do, what is refused, the [wasm] manifest section, erp addon build/package/install, and the data files a package may ship. Use when the user wants an addon that installs into a running server as an .erpaddon file instead of a compiled-in native addon.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-wizards-actions/SKILL.md`: Build transient wizard dialogs and custom full-screen client actions in an ERPForAll addon - transient models with <footer> confirm/cancel buttons, bounded act_window and display_notification action results, transient cleanup policy (transient_max_age_seconds), and ir.actions.client tags with ClientActionDecl and registerClientAction. Use when an object button opens a multi-field modal dialog or a menu opens a custom board or workspace.

Tools (Python 3.11+): `python3 {{KIT}}/tools/new-addon.py <name> --dest addons` scaffolds a data-only
addon; `python3 {{KIT}}/tools/addon-lint.py addons/<name> --addons-path addons` checks one;
`python3 {{KIT}}/tools/addon-graph.py context "<task>"` lists what your addons define before you write against it;
`python3 {{KIT}}/tools/test-levels.py basic|normal|advanced` runs a test level in a checkout of the framework.
If a skill does not cover something, say so; do not invent APIs, XML attributes or CLI flags.
